  "codebook": {
    "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator explicitly or implicitly takes personal responsibility for a specific action, outcome, or achievement, often highlighting their direct role in securing funding, passing legislation, or influencing policy decisions.",
    "clarification": "Credit-claiming is identified when the senator uses first-person language (e.g., 'I secured,' 'I authored,' 'I helped') or when the text explicitly attributes an action or outcome to the senator's efforts. This includes announcements of funding, legislative achievements, or recognition of their role in a process. The focus is on the senator's personal involvement and the tangible or intangible benefits they claim to have delivered.",
